In the context of CDEs, the data consists of multiple xx : [s0, sn] → Rdx that need to be batched together. In principle each interval [s0, sn] may be different for each batch element, for example if we chose sj = tj and the data is irregularly sampled.
Batchable differential equation solvers Some (very few) differential equation software libraries allow batching over different regions of integration. In this case the problem is straightforward: simply use the capabilities of the library. For example this is the case with Diffrax [Kid21a].
Other differential equation solvers Most differential equation software libraries do not intrinsically support batching over different regions of integration. For example this is the case with torchdiffeq and torchcde [Che18; Kid20].
