(Typically we actually observe xtrue only at some discretised time stamps; not over a full continuous-time path. For ease of presentation we neglect this detail for now and will return to it later.)
Let w : [0, T ] → Rdw be a dw-dimensional Brownian motion, and let v ∼ N (0, Idv×dv ) be drawn from a dv-dimensional standard multivariate normal. The values dw, dv ∈ N are hyperparameters describing the size of the noise. Let
