One effective simplification is to take dw = dy and parameterise the diffusion σθ as a diagonal matrix. This is cheap to compute the inverse of: take the reciprocal of each diagonal element.
For numerical stability it is additionally often desirable to then bound these diagonal elements away from zero: use z 7→ sigmoid(z) + 10−4 as a final nonlinearity for σθ, or alternatively clamp any values in the range [−10−6, 10−6] to the edges of that range.
